%S A296626 1,2,6,14,34,74,164,342,714,1442,2894,5686,11096,21322,40688,76770,
%T A296626 143890,267294,493558,904710,1649386,2988618,5388784,9665490,17259960,
%U A296626 30680166,54317658,95776106,168266544,294549042,513902596,893670334,1549381050,2678193698,4616533666,7936025862
%N A296626 a(n) is the total multiplicity of all products of Schur functions s(lambda)*s(mu) with size(lambda) + size(mu) = n.
%C A296626 Equals 2*A296624 - aerated version of A296625, so s(lambda)*s(mu) is counted again as s(mu)*s(lambda) if mu <> lambda. The aerated version of A296625 reads as 1, 0, 2, 0, 6, 0, 16, 0, 42, 0, 106, 0, ...
%H A296626 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A296626/b296626.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%F A296626 a(0) = 1; a(n) = (1/n) * Sum_{j=1..n} b(j) * a(n-j), where b(n) = Sum_{d|n/2} d * 2^(n/(2*d)) + Sum_{d|n, d odd} (n/d) * c(n/d), c(m) = 2^((m+1)/2) for odd m and c(m) = 3 * 2^(m/2-1) for even m. The first sum in b(n) is zero for odd n. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 14 2026
%Y A296626 For a program see A296624 and A296625.
%K A296626 nonn,changed
%O A296626 0,2
%A A296626 _Wouter Meeussen_, Dec 17 2017
%E A296626 a(15) onward from _Vladeta Jovovic_, Oct 14 2026
